        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 9:30PM PDT until September 25 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Seattle WA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Northwest winds 20 to 30 kt and seas 9 to 14 ft.

* WHERE...Coastal Waters From Cape Flattery To James Island Out
10 Nm, Coastal Waters From James Island To Point Grenville Out
10 Nm, Coastal Waters From Cape Flattery To James Island 10 To
60 Nm and Coastal Waters From James Island To Point Grenville
10 To 60 Nm.

* WHEN...From 5 AM to 11 PM PDT Friday.

* IMPACTS...Conditions will be hazardous to small craft.
</description>
        <instruction>A Small Craft Advisory means that wind speeds of 21 to 33 knots
and/or seas 10 feet or higher are expected to produce hazardous
wave conditions to small craft. Inexperienced mariners,
especially those operating smaller vessels should avoid
navigating in these conditions.</instruction>
